2fta|v|To turn up, or delve in, (earth) with a spade or a hoe; to open, loosen, or break up (the soil) with a spade, or other sharp instrument; to pierce, open, or loosen, as if with a spade. ; To get by digging; as, to dig potatoes, or gold. ; To hollow out, as a well; to form, as a ditch, by removing earth; to excavate; as, to dig a ditch or a well. ; To thrust; to poke. ; To work with a spade or other like implement; to do servile work; to delve. ; To take ore from its bed, in distinction from making excavations in search of ore. ; To work like a digger; to study ploddingly and laboriously. ; A plodding and laborious student.	o:27ti,111,6;2glv,92,19;9u3l,84,37;2jar,82,11;54vm,78,1;2k4p,63,4;pm4,58,2;arvv,57,1;9wih,55,25;8bau,54,6;2fuq,43,1;3uc2,43,4;44oh,41,123;4ngf,41,4;2l3e,37,3~fk7,3,158;44oh,41,123;9u3l,84,37;9wih,55,25;9mpa,30,25;2glv,92,19;2jar,82,11;6g20,9,10;a17k,13,8;9xj0,8,8;8bau,54,6;27ti,111,6;aibv,31,5;2k4p,63,4;3uc2,43,4	s:1gq8,83,27;2k5t,80,6;i1k,74,10;8zga,60,8;7z2u,39,4;5xeo,35,8;56s5,28,2;8n0e,22,1;57ad,19,78;66jl,15,2;3sp6,12,13;4bop,5,5;3t7w,3,2~57ad,19,78;1gq8,83,27;3sp6,12,13;i1k,74,10;8zga,60,8;5xeo,35,8;2k5t,80,6;4bop,5,5;7z2u,39,4;3t7w,3,2;56s5,28,2;66jl,15,2;8n0e,22,1	d:6ulj,62,9;3qvz,34,10;1a8z,28,53;3qrl,24,1;7rn5,12,626;5jox,10,75;2qfd,10,107;29ot,10,76;7f56,8,305;9rhn,6,32;31jk,3,25;7nk2,1,22~7rn5,12,626;7f56,8,305;2qfd,10,107;29ot,10,76;5jox,10,75;1a8z,28,53;9rhn,6,32;31jk,3,25;7nk2,1,22;3qvz,34,10;6ulj,62,9;3qrl,24,1	D:2906,54,528;291h,51,87;290z,40,82;a14z,30,8;66jk,15,3;9qej,15,454;944x,14,54;a4pc,14,1198;3j42,12,122;j3w,12,286~a4pc,14,1198;2906,54,528;9qej,15,454;j3w,12,286;3j42,12,122;291h,51,87;290z,40,82;944x,14,54;a14z,30,8;66jk,15,3
