2gmj|n|An extensive order of insects having only two functional wings and two balancers, as the house fly, mosquito, etc. They have a suctorial proboscis, often including two pairs of sharp organs (mandibles and maxillae) with which they pierce the skin of animals. They undergo a complete metamorphosis, their larvae (called maggots) being usually without feet.	a:6r1c,24,5~6r1c,24,5	v:6phi,17,1~6phi,17,1	V:35yb,70,4~35yb,70,4	n:4irq,217,32;3cko,113,4;6phi,40,5~4irq,217,32;6phi,40,5;3cko,113,4	N:1h7w,236,50;3cko,108,3~1h7w,236,50;3cko,108,3
